      <sectiondef kind="func">
      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__xwdttb__winwdt__qamode__example_1gad5e60e9f326186ec41039b1ad536e60d" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int WdtTbIntrExample</definition>
        <argsstring>(XWdtTb *WdtTbInstancePtr, UINTPTR BaseAddress)</argsstring>
        <name>WdtTbIntrExample</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="struct_x_wdt_tb" kindref="compound">XWdtTb</ref> *</type>
          <declname>WdtTbInstancePtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>UINTPTR</type>
          <declname>BaseAddress</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Demonstrates the functioning of the Window Watchdog QA mode. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function sets up WWDT in QA mode, enables interrupt subsystem. It programs the first (closed) and second (window) and sets up an interrupt to raise an interrupt in the open window. In the closed window the function writes three correct responses to the relevant Token_Resp register. Once the interrupt is received in the open window, it writes the 4th correct response to the Token_resp register. The last (fourth) write ends the second (open window).</para><para>This function assumes that the reset output of the Window Watchdog Timer is not connected to the reset of the processor. The function allows the Window Watchdog Timer to timeout such that a reset occurs if it is connected.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">WdtTbInstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the instance of WdtTb driver. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">BaseAddress</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Base address of the device.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS if interrupt example run successfully.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_FAILURE, if reset has occurred.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>In XSCT/classic flow, the example uses WdtTbDeviceId and WdtTbIntrId to look up the device configuration and set up interrupt handling. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="/proj/xhdsswstaff1/bhawanas/patch_integration/auto_jobs/esw_github_doxy/git/2026.2/embeddedsw/XilinxProcessorIPLib/drivers/wdttb/examples/xwdttb_winwdt_qamode_example.c" line="140" column="1"/>
